<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof for Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmprop1" title="Proposition 2.1 (Increase of LLM-MAS Performance Gain with Depth 𝑑 and Width 𝑤). ‣ 2.2 Task Complexity for LLM-MAS Effectiveness ‣ 2 Analysis Framework ‣ On the Importance of Task Complexity in Evaluating LLM-Based Multi-Agent Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(d,w,N,r)\;\triangleq\;\frac{S_{\mathrm{multi}}-S_{\mathrm{single}}}{S_{\mathrm{single}}}\;=\;\left(\frac{r\,[1-(1-s(w))^{N}]}{s(w)}\right)^{d}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≜</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>multi</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>single</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>single</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(d,w,N,r)\;\triangleq\;\frac{S_{\mathrm{multi}}-S_{\mathrm{single}}}{S_{\mathrm{single}}}\;=\;\left(\frac{r\,[1-(1-s(w))^{N}]}{s(w)}\right)^{d}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=s(w)=q^{w}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=s(w)=q^{w}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and define:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(s)\triangleq r\bigl[1-(1-s)^{N}\bigr],\quad f(s)\triangleq\frac{A(s)}{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(s)\triangleq r\bigl[1-(1-s)^{N}\bigr],\quad f(s)\triangleq\frac{A(s)}{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(d,w,N,r)=f(s)^{d}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(d,w,N,r)=f(s)^{d}-1</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, by assumption, we have <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(s)=\frac{A(s)}{s}&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(s)=\frac{A(s)}{s}&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, for the partial derivative in <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\Delta}{\partial d}=\ln(f(s))\,f(s)^{d}&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\Delta}{\partial d}=\ln(f(s))\,f(s)^{d}&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">For the partial derivative in <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\Delta}{\partial w}=d\,f(s)^{d-1}\,f^{\prime}(s)\,s^{\prime}(w)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\Delta}{\partial w}=d\,f(s)^{d-1}\,f^{\prime}(s)\,s^{\prime}(w).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1-s\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1-s\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}(s)s-A(s)=r\left[Ns(1-s)^{N-1}-(1-(1-s)^{N})\right]=-r\left(1-t^{N}-N(1-t)t^{N-1}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}(s)s-A(s)=r\left[Ns(1-s)^{N-1}-(1-(1-s)^{N})\right]=-r\left(1-t^{N}-N(1-t)t^{N-1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">By the Mean Value Theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite> applied to <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x)=x^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x)=x^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[t,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[t,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\in(t,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\in(t,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-t^{N}=N\xi^{N-1}(1-t)\geq Nt^{N-1}(1-t)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-t^{N}=N\xi^{N-1}(1-t)\geq Nt^{N-1}(1-t).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">Thus the bracketed expression is nonnegative, making <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\prime}(s)s-A(s)\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\prime}(s)s-A(s)\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(s)=\frac{A^{\prime}(s)s-A(s)}{s^{2}}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(s)=\frac{A^{\prime}(s)s-A(s)}{s^{2}}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}(w)=q^{w}\ln q&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}(w)=q^{w}\ln q&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\Delta}{\partial w}=d\,f(s)^{d-1}\,f^{\prime}(s)\,s^{\prime}(w)&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\Delta}{\partial w}=d\,f(s)^{d-1}\,f^{\prime}(s)\,s^{\prime}(w)&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof for Proposition <a href="#S2.Thmprop2" title="Proposition 2.2 (Unbounded Growth in Depth vs. Finite Saturation in Width). ‣ 2.2 Task Complexity for LLM-MAS Effectiveness ‣ 2 Analysis Framework ‣ On the Importance of Task Complexity in Evaluating LLM-Based Multi-Agent Systems" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(d,w,N,r)\;\triangleq\;\frac{S_{\mathrm{multi}}-S_{\mathrm{single}}}{S_{\mathrm{single}}}\;=\;\left(\frac{r\,[1-(1-s(w))^{N}]}{s(w)}\right)^{d}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≜</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>multi</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>single</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>single</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(d,w,N,r)\;\triangleq\;\frac{S_{\mathrm{multi}}-S_{\mathrm{single}}}{S_{\mathrm{single}}}\;=\;\left(\frac{r\,[1-(1-s(w))^{N}]}{s(w)}\right)^{d}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=s(w)=q^{w}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=s(w)=q^{w}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and define:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(s)\triangleq r\bigl[1-(1-s)^{N}\bigr],\quad f(s)\triangleq\frac{A(s)}{s}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(s)\triangleq r\bigl[1-(1-s)^{N}\bigr],\quad f(s)\triangleq\frac{A(s)}{s}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">As <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(w)=q^{w}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(w)=q^{w}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. By the Binomial Theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>, for integer <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-s)^{N}=1-Ns+\binom{N}{2}s^{2}-\dots+(-s)^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-s)^{N}=1-Ns+\binom{N}{2}s^{2}-\dots+(-s)^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we can have the following representation: <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-(1-s)^{N}=Ns+O(s^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-(1-s)^{N}=Ns+O(s^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math> Therefore, we can have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{w\to\infty}\Delta(d,w,N,r)=(rN)^{d}-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{w\to\infty}\Delta(d,w,N,r)=(rN)^{d}-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(s)&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(s)&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(s)^{d}\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(s)^{d}\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\to+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\to+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, therefore we can have:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{d\to\infty}\Delta(d,w,N,r)=+\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{d\to\infty}\Delta(d,w,N,r)=+\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Experimental Results</h2>

<figure id="A3.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04311v1/math_accs_multi.png" id="A3.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:429/740;" width="429" height="740" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A3.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The accuracy of LLM-SAS and LLM-MAS on math reasoning.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04311v1/writing_accs_multi.png" id="A3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/511;" width="476" height="511" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="A3.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The writing score of LLM-SAS and LLM-MAS on creative writing.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
